    <md:title>2.9.3: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>086109e0-3e90-4188-bcd7-d6e4c40fb658</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section>
    <para dir="ltr">A water park charges $17 per entry plus a $40 fee for raft rentals. An amusement park charges a $21 entry fee.For the number of entries, \(e\), which inequality represents the total cost of the water park being less than the total cost of the amusement park?</para>
  </section>
</content>
</document>
